What are embeddings?

Embeddings are numerical vector representations of data such as text. They capture semantic information and allow systems to compare meaning mathematically.

Q2. Why are embeddings important in RAG?

Embeddings convert document chunks and user queries into vectors. The system compares these vectors to retrieve semantically relevant document chunks, which are then passed to an LLM as context.

Q3. What is the difference between keyword search and semantic search?

Keyword search looks for matching words or terms. Semantic search looks for similarity in meaning using embeddings.

Q4. What is cosine similarity?

Cosine similarity measures the cosine of the angle between two vectors. It is commonly used to compare embedding vectors.



