Q5. Does an embedding model generate answers?

No. Its primary purpose is to generate vector representations. An LLM generally generates the final natural-language response.

Q6. What is embedding dimension?

It is the number of numerical values in an embedding vector. For example, a 384-dimensional embedding contains 384 numbers.

Q7. Can we use different embedding models for document ingestion and query processing?

It is generally best to use the same embedding model and compatible configuration for both. Otherwise, the vectors may not be comparable in the intended way. If the embedding model changes, the document vectors normally need to be regenerated.

