I would troubleshoot the issue systematically across the RAG pipeline.
First, I would inspect the customer query to verify whether the system correctly identifies the loan type as a personal loan and the intent as prepayment.
Second, I would check document extraction and chunking to ensure that personal loan and home loan policies are stored as separate, meaningful chunks.
Third, I would verify the embedding model, dimensions and document-to-vector mapping to ensure that query and document embeddings are compatible.
Next, I would inspect the vector database metadata and similarity scores. Since the query specifically mentions a personal loan, I would apply metadata filtering using the loan_type field so that only personal loan documents are considered during retrieval.
I would also consider adding a reranking model to improve the relevance of the retrieved documents.
Finally, I would validate the context passed to the LLM and ensure that it answers only from the correct policy document. If the relevant policy is unavailable, the chatbot should not generate unsupported information.
I would test the solution using multiple personal loan and home loan queries and monitor retrieval accuracy to ensure that the issue is resolved.

